 <section class="occ-guide" id="occ-guide" hidden><strong>Your first shift</strong><p>Keep trams moving and road queues below 65 seconds for five simulated minutes. Select a junction on the map to see why it changes. Select a tram to set its speed, hold it, skip a stop, or terminate its service. Requests always pass through the signal clearance sequence. The balance slider gives trams a stronger voice, not an unconditional green.</p><p>Green = proceed, amber = clearing, red = stop. Pedestrians have a separate protected stage. CCTV shows the same live 3D vehicles as the map. Engineering view reveals scores, detector occupancy and all timing parameters. This is a game interpretation, with finite recycled road traffic and terminal-only turnbacks.</p></section>
